  "note": "Registers per thread and block size as the profiled run chose them; ClimaCore sizes the block from the register count, so both move together and occupancy is derived from the pair. A kernel's mean is over its own launches, and `name_covers_variants` > 1 means the reported figures are the heaviest variant of a shared name. `registers_for_next_step` is what the kernel would have to reach for one more block per SM, which is the gap a fold has to close to pay. `device_total` is every kernel in the arm and so includes any other treatment the mod arm carries; `fold_attributable` is the subtotal over the kernels listed here, which is the fold's own share. It is name-paired, so it drops any kernel whose name the fold merged --- `device_saving` is the one to divide by, since it takes the family total wherever a target is unpaired and names the basis it used.",
